# Domain libraries

- Pure functions. No I/O. No side effects while a module loads, other than building indexes and data-integrity guards (D-05, D-18).
- `plate-domain` depends only on `plate-data`. No other runtime dependency (D-05).
- Do not hardcode plate codes. Code tables are derived from `plate-data` (D-38). The § 30 ust. 1 alphabet and the five § 25 plate types stay in `plate-domain`; they are not registry fields (D-07).
- JSDoc on a public export states the contract: inputs, result variants, invariants. A legal citation is the provision plus its row ID from `docs/pl-plate-rules.md` (D-33, D-41).
